e>Coupling behavior of the cervical spine: a systematic review of the literature</article-title><source>J Manipulative Physiol Ther</source><year>2006</year><volume>29</volume><fpage>570</fpage><lpage>575</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16949947</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.jmpt.2006.06.020</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B26"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ishii</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Mukai</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Hosono</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Sakaura</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Fujii</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Nakajima</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><etal></etal></person-group><article-title>Kinematics of the cervical spine in lateral bending: in vivo three-dimensional analysis</article-title><source>Spine</source><year>2006</year><volume>31</volume><fpage>155</fpage><lpage>160</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16418633</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1097/01.brs.0000195173.47334.1f</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B27"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Malmstrom</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Karlberg</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Fransson</surname><given-names>PA</given-names></name><name><surname>Melander</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Magnusson</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Primary and Coupled Cervical Movements. The Effect of Age, Gender, and Body Mass Index. A 3-Dimensional Movement Analysis of a Population Without Symptoms of Neck Disorders</article-title><source>Spine</source><year>2006</year><volume>31</volume><fpage>E44</fpage><lpage>E50</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16418624</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="do